+### A port's own pages (gp main20m)
+
+`xbox_OverlaySetPortPages(n, ops)` (`xbox_settings.h`) adds up to two pages of the port's own rows, first in the tabs.
+The port keeps the model; every frame the overlay asks for the rows (`rows`, `row`: an item with a label, a value - a
+status chip, or a choice with arrows - and a hint; a section header; a wrapped paragraph; a line of small text) and hands
+it the actions on the selected row (`input`: A, left, right, X, Y, B; the answer says whether it acted, asked, changed
+view or did nothing, which picks the sound). There is no row limit (up to `XBOX_PORT_ROWS`, drawn only where in view);
+a label too long for its column shrinks to 72 %, and on the selected row then scrolls (a second's hold, along, a
+second's hold); other rows end it with an ellipsis. The footer shows the pad's or the keyboard's prompts with the
+port's word for each button on that row; LT / RT jump a screen of rows. The port's pending changes (`restart`) are
+counted in "Restart now to apply N changes"; `xbox_OverlayRequestOpenPage` opens the overlay on a port page (as the
+title's menu entry does), `xbox_OverlayShowPortPage` switches to one, `xbox_OverlayRestartNow` restarts as the pinned
+row does. The callbacks run on the overlay's thread with its lock held. No page registered: the overlay as before.
+Burnout 3: the Mods and Mod settings pages (`src/game/modsmenu_ov.c`).
+
 ### Restart now and Quit game (the foot of every page)
 
